{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
  "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The court of appeals in this case made two fundamental and separate errors, each of which should require reversal of its decision. First, all agree that the question whether Title IX precludes the use of Section 1983 to enforce the Constitution is a matter of congressional intent. Yet, the court of appeals entirely disregarded all of the ordinary indicia of congressional intent: The statutory text, the statutory background structure and evolution, the unquestioned legislative purpose. Each of these considerations points conclusively towards a single outcome: Congress did not mean Title IX to preclude the use of Section 1983 to enforce the Constitution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What more? What more is alleged in the complaint?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Mr. Rothfeld)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so, at the time that Congress used the language of Title IX, it knew that that language had been uniformly, widely construed across the country to allow the simultaneous assertion of those claims, not the preclusion of Section 1983 claims for discrimination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Title IX is Spending Clause legislation, and that, under our precedents, imposes certain limitations on how we interpret it that would not be applicable under Section 1983."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: I take it they don't have to bring these actions together. They can sue under Title IX; if they lose, then they can start a whole new lawsuit under 1983?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Would you go over that again? I didn't understand it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Barnstable School Committee (Respondents)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Therefore, having Title IX preclude section 1983 Equal Protection claims does not deny petitioners in this or any other case availability --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Hodge",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HODGE: Well, I would argue -- I would argue to the Court that I would hope that this Court would take -- would affirm the First Circuit opinion, but I would say to -- to -- to Your Honor the following: that with regard to the individual defendant in this case, who is the superintendent of schools, who as we argue, the question presented only deals with the institutional recipient; but nevertheless the First Circuit found that the individual was acting only in their official capacity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: So you were saying if it's an individual acting in his official capacity, you cannot sue him under Title IX?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: He says there is an issue in controversy, that's good enough for me."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1125",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5ba8236018af0be790c427300241a02c9d8e9281340b7c63effa113b104024f8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5ba8236018af-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
